{"__module__": "langchain.schema.messages", "__name__": "ChatMessage", "id": "379966a9b46d4b45bce743258a909dc6", "name": "user", "role": "user", "content": "\nYou are a geisoscientist, and you need to use tools to answer multiple-choice questions about Earth observation data analysis. Note that if a tool returns an error, you can only try again once. Ultimately, you only need to explicitly tell me the correct choice.\nATTENTION:\n1. When a tool returns \"Result saved at /path/to/file\", you must use the full returned path \"/path/to/file\" in all subsequent tool calls.\n2. For each question, you must provide the choice you think is most appropriate.Don't gibe me another format. Your final answer format must be:\n<Answer>Your choice<Answer>\n3. Before accessing any file in a data directory, always call get_filelist on that directory first to discover the actual filenames. Never assume or guess filenames.\n\n\nQuestion: Using Landsat 8 Band 10 and reflectance bands (Red and NIR) over New York City for June–July of 2020 and 2021, estimate LST using the NDVI-based single-channel method. Compute the proportion of pixels with LST > 305 K for each year, then calculate the absolute difference between the two yearly values.benchmark/data/question99\nA.0.80%\nB.0.50%\nC.1.50%\nD.1.80%", "metadata": {"question_id": "99"}, "timestamp": "2026-07-03 21:08:27"}
{"__module__": "langchain.schema.messages", "__name__": "ChatMessage", "id": "58b7bd6cb5104c99919c68185c463ab9", "name": "99", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "To answer this question, I will follow these steps:\n\n1. List the files in the directory `benchmark/data/question99`.\n2. Identify the relevant files for Landsat 8 Band 10, Red, and NIR bands for June–July of 2020 and 2021.\n3. Use the `lst_single_channel` function to estimate LST for each year.\n4. Use the `count_above_threshold` function to compute the proportion of pixels with LST > 305 K for each year.\n5. Calculate the absolute difference between the two yearly values.\n\nLet's start by listing the files in the directory."}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "AivuDKPYM", "name": "get_filelist", "input": {"dir_path": "benchmark/data/question99"}}], "metadata": null, "timestamp": "2026-07-03 21:12:49"}
